# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element, after the closing `</AuthProvider>` tag

This placement ensures analytics tracking is active across all pages while maintaining the existing layout structure.

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Used the framework-specific import path `@vercel/analytics/next` for Next.js App Router
- Positioned the Analytics component in the root layout file for site-wide tracking
- Preserved all existing code structure, imports, and components

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ No new linting errors introduced by the changes
✅ Lock files updated appropriately
✅ All staged changes are source code only (no build artifacts)

## Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel project dashboard (Analytics section)
3. After deployment, analytics data will begin collecting automatically

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated dependency lock file
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
